/**
 * @page dev_freq_config Device frequency configuration
 * 
 * @if DOX_NAV
 * @ref dev_config "Back to the list of SDR device configuration sub-topics" 
 * @endif
 * 
 * Optionally, it is possible to view and set extra SDR device clock values. The amount of adjustable clock generators on a SDR device, depends on a SDR device model and onboard modules. SDR devices that use LMS7002M 
 * module contains the following clocks:
 * <ul>
 *    <li>Reference clock. ID - 0</li>
 *    <li>Rx synthsizer (Rx LO) clock. ID - 1</li>
 *    <li>Tx synthesizer (Tx LO) clock. ID - 2</li>
 *    <li>Core clock. ID - 3</li>
 *    <li>Rx transceiver signal processor (RXTSP) clock. ID - 4</li>
 *    <li>Tx transceiver signal processor (TXTSP) clock. ID - 5</li>
 * </ul>
 * 
 * To view a specific clock frequency, use @ref lime::SDRDevice::GetClockFreq(uint8_t, uint8_t) "GetClockFreq()" function. To set a specific clock frequency, use @ref lime::SDRDevice::SetClockFreq(uint8_t, double, uint8_t)
 * "SetClockFreq()" function. Here is an output of different clock values for LimeSDR Mini V2.4 device (example code below):
 * 
 * @image{inline} html dev_freq_config.png
 * 
 * @section ref_clock Reference clock
 * 
 * <b>It is recommended to avoid the modification of reference clock frequency</b>
 * 
 * Reference clock is an external clock signal source used for synchronization of internal clock generators. Reference clock value must be set to the exact value of the reference clock that is present on SDR device
 * board. Different SDR devices can support different reference clock frequencies. Refer to the respective SDR device hardware data sheets for supported reference clock ranges.
 * 
 * @section sx_clock Synthesizer clocks
 * 
 * Rx or Tx synthesizer (SX) clocks control the LO frequency for each direction. For SDR devices with LMS7002M module, LO frequency modification is independent of a selected channel. Therefore, setting SX clock for a 
 * specific direction on a specific channel, will set the LO frequency for the specified direction on all channels.
 * 
 * @important It is recommended to use alternative LO frequency modification functions, that are described in @ref lo_freq section of @ref generic_config sub-topic.
 * 
 * @section tsp_clocks TSP clocks
 * 
 * Rx and Tx TSP clocks are read only and cannot be modified. The clock values are automatically derived on start up from the Core clock value.
 * 
 * @section core_clk Core clock
 * 
 * Core clock is the main device clock that is used as a source to derive the clock values for internal components (ADCs, NCOs, TSPs and etc.) of SDR device module(s). <b>Modification of Core clock will alter the SDR device 
 * performance</b>.
 * 
 * @section clock_example Exmaple code
 * 
 * Example code for retrieving various clock values of LimeSDR Mini V2.4 device:
 * 
 * @code{.cpp}
 * #include <iostream>
 * #include <vector>
 * #include <cinttypes>
 * #include <limesuiteng/DeviceRegistry.h>
 * #include <limesuiteng/SDRDevice.h>
 * #include <limesuiteng/DeviceHandle.h>
 * #include <limesuiteng/OpStatus.h>
 * #include <limesuiteng/SDRDescriptor.h>
 * 
 * int main()
 * {
 *    std::vector<lime::DeviceHandle> listOfDevices = lime::DeviceRegistry::enumerate();
 *    if(listOfDevices.empty())
 *    {
 *       std::cout << "No devices detected!\n";
 *       return 0;
 *    }
 * 
 *    lime::SDRDevice * device = lime::DeviceRegistry::makeDevice(listOfDevices.front());
 *    if(device == nullptr)
 *    {
 *       std::cout << "Failed to connect to SDR device\n";
 *       return 1;
 *    }
 * 
 *    uint8_t moduleIndex = 0;
 *    uint8_t ChA = 0;
 *    uint8_t CLK_REF = 0;
 *    uint8_t CLK_SXR = 1;
 *    uint8_t CLK_SXT = 2;
 *    uint8_t CLK_CGEN = 3;
 *    uint8_t CLK_RXTSP = 4;
 *    uint8_t CLK_TXTSP = 5;
 *    lime::SDRDescriptor LimeMiniDesc;
 * 
 *    LimeMiniDesc = device->GetDescriptor();
 *    std::cout << LimeMiniDesc.name << " device supported clocks and default frequency values:\n";
 *    std::cout << "REF clock " << device->GetClockFreq(CLK_REF, ChA)   << " Hz\n";
 *    std::cout << "SXR clock " << device->GetClockFreq(CLK_SXR, ChA)   << " Hz\n";
 *    std::cout << "SXT clock " << device->GetClockFreq(CLK_SXT, ChA)   << " Hz\n";
 *    std::cout << "CGEN clock " << device->GetClockFreq(CLK_CGEN, ChA)  << " Hz\n";
 *    std::cout << "RXTSP clock (Read only)" << device->GetClockFreq(CLK_RXTSP, ChA) << " Hz\n";
 *    std::cout << "TXTSP clock (Read only)" << device->GetClockFreq(CLK_TXTSP, ChA) << " Hz\n";
 * 
 *    lime::DeviceRegistry::freeDevice(device);
 *    return 0;
 * }
 * @endcode
 */